# NEGATIVE CONTROL for eventually_ (expected-failure script).
# The runner treats a `fail_` prefix as expected-to-fail: this script
# PASSES the batch only if the command below actually FAILS. The
# condition can never become true (spawning is off, no agents), so a
# correct eventually_ implementation fails it after the 2s timeout.
# If the timeout path silently consumed instead of failing, this
# script would (incorrectly) pass its assertion and the batch would
# report this script as FAILED — that is the control firing.
reset_game
set_spawn_enabled 0
wait_frames 5
eventually_assert 2 assert_agent_count gte 1
